# Spec: Special Flows via SQLite migrations

## Goal
Replace open-time catalog kludges with a versioned in-process migration runner, then make Special Flows a real section.

## Behavior
1. `schema_migrations` table + ordered TS `up(db)` steps on openCatalog.
2. Migration: create catalog tables (nullable section_id); rebuild if NOT NULL.
3. Migration: insert section special-flow / Special Flows; attach attack-series, ramey-flow, marvin-flow, preschool-flow.
4. Delete every-open detachNamedFlows null UPDATE.
5. Keep seed.sql unchanged; seedIfEmpty after schema migrate.
6. createSection: letter uppercased; dashed ids lowercase.
7. nextWarmupId: dashed section ids mint special-flow-1 style.
8. Admin/home/schedule: Named Flows → Special Flows / #special-flow; A-H schedule unchanged.
9. Characterization tests: green before refactor; after, only intentional Special Flows deltas change.

## Out of scope
Slug warmup renames; schedule SeriesId beyond A-H; client localStorage shims; down migrations.